        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "G6gDTn",
          "name": "Rules",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": "$space-3",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "kpGTr",
              "name": "section head",
              "gap": "$space-3",
              "alignItems": "center",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "hE0zp",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$text",
                  "content": "Rules",
                  "lineHeight": 1.3,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-heading",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "fPuQO",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$faint",
                  "content": "each rule with its token; the page follows design/foundation.md for the rest",
                  "lineHeight": 1.3,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "r37FA",
              "name": "rules",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": "$space-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JDAKS",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "1. Two columns at 1200: a sidebar of 280 px with a 1 px $border at its right, and the editor; the sidebar shows the tree or the git panel on `[x] files [ ] git 3`, N the count of `git status` rows; at 390 three tabs `[ ] files [x] edit [ ] git 3` in the same radio idiom, the active tab full width.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "O6OsU",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "2. Header bar: 44 px on $bg with a 1 px $border under it; `kitterm /` in $muted and the path in $text at $type-heading 13 px; the buffer state after it; the facts `TypeScript · LF · UTF-8` in $faint at $type-body; `[ save ⌘S ]` and `open in terminal` in $accent at the right; `[ save ]` alone at 390.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "wqYIc",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "3. Buffer state, one run of text in the mark's colour: nothing while the buffer equals the disk and `[ save ⌘S ]` in $faint; `● edited` in $warning while it differs; `◐ saving` in $accent (the one turning mark) during the PUT; `✓ saved` in $success until the next edit; `– read only` in $faint with the save control in $faint.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "xwRBa",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "4. Tree rows: $line-compact 28 px at 1200, $line-touch 44 px at 390; $space-3 per level; the triangle in $faint at $mark-size-disclosure 11 px, `▼` open and `▶` closed, one level per expand (one GET /api/files per folder); the name in $text at $type-body; the open file's row on $surface-2; ignored files are not listed.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "D6XEhL",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "5. Badges at the right of a row from one `git status --porcelain=v2 -z`: `M` $warning, `A` $success, `D` $danger, `?` $faint for an untracked file; a folder wears the badge of the changed path under it; no badge in a clean tree.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "XjCJO",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "6. Editor: CodeMirror 6 on $sunken, $mono at $md-code 12.5 px with a line height of 1.6 (20 px); the gutter 48 px wide (36 at 390) with the number in $faint, right aligned, a 1 px $border at its right; the source view's colours: $code-keyword, $code-string, $code-comment, $code-number, $code-name, $code-punct.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Dz8sD",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "7. Git panel: a label per section in $faint at $type-body weight 600 (`BRANCH`, `CHANGES 3`, `COMMIT`); the branch name in $text with `↑1 ↓0` in $muted (ahead, behind origin); one row per changed file: the stage toggle `[ ]`/`[x]` in $text, the badge, the name, `+21 −1` in $muted; the selected row on $surface-2; the message box on $surface with a 1 px $border; `[ commit ]` `[ push ]` in $accent.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "I2jVJL",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "8. Stage control: the `[ ]`/`[x]` toggle on the row is the stage; a tap on the toggle stages or unstages the whole file (hunks stay in lazygit); `CHANGES 3 · 2 staged` counts the checked rows; the commit takes the checked rows and nothing else; a row with nothing checked leaves `[ commit ]` in $faint.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "J7qO4o",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "9. Diff: a tap on the name of a change row shows its unified diff in the editor area, read only: the hunk line `@@ -64,6 +64,10 @@` in $code-link, a `+` line in $success, a `−` line in $danger, context in $text; the gutter prints the new file's numbers and nothing on a `−` line; `open file` in $accent at the right of the top line returns to the buffer; at 390 the diff opens in the edit tab.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "gvU9N",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "10. Bars under the header, 44 px on $surface with a 1 px $border under: the mark, one sentence in $text, the controls in $accent; `?` $warning `Changed on disk since you opened it. [ reload ] [ compare ] [ keep mine ]`; `!` $danger `Not saved: changed on disk since you opened it. [ reload ] [ compare ] [ keep mine ]` (the 412); reload takes the disk's bytes, compare shows the diff of the buffer against the disk, keep mine takes the disk's hash as the base so the next save writes over it.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "eLT2a",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "11. Read only, the sentence in the bar with `–` $faint: `Read only: 1.2 MB, the first 256 KB shown. A save would drop the rest.` (X-Kitterm-Truncated); `Read only: not text (image/png).`; `Read only: the bytes are not UTF-8.`; over the cap nothing opens: `Cannot read file-preview.ts: the daemon answered 413: file over 262144 bytes.` (the words of markdown-view.ts).",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Xr1r8",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "12. Empty tree: the root row and under it one sentence in $faint at the row's indent, `src is empty.`; a tree with no project root prints `No project here: open /edit from a shell inside a checkout.`",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "p8rYf",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "13. A git command that failed: a line under the buttons with `!` $danger and the first stderr line in $muted, `git push exited 1: ! [rejected] goal/code-editor -> goal/code-editor (fetch first)`, the shape of `gh pr list exited <code>: <first stderr line>`; it stays until the next command.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Cc0TX",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "14. In flight: the button is replaced by `◐ pushing` or `◐ committing` (`◐` $accent, the one thing that moves, the word in $muted); a commit's hook output lands in a well on $sunken with a 1 px $border under the word, one line per stderr line in $faint, at most the last 8, until the commit ends.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ra94h",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "15. The phone: $line-touch 44 px rows and targets; with the soft keyboard open a 44 px bar on $surface with a 1 px $border above it sits over the keyboard and holds `[ save ]` in $accent, `tab ↑ ↓ ← →` and `undo` in $muted, each a 44 px target; the editor keeps the space above it.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Z3UPv",
                  "name": "t",
                  "fill": "$muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "16. The terminal idiom: $mono everywhere, hairlines in $border, no radius above 2 px, no shadow, no transition; the owned colours paint a mark, a badge, the diff's `+` and `−` lines and the one run of text that carries a state, never a background; `--ui-*` tokens so the page follows the terminal theme.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$mono",
                  "fontSize": "$type-body",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
